      "text": "To determine when Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will all be working together again, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their work schedules. Darren works every 3rd school day, so his schedule is \\( \\text{lcm}(1, 3) = 3 \\). Wanda works every 4th school day, so her schedule is \\( \\text{lcm}(1, 4) = 4 \\). Beatrice works every 6th school day, so her schedule is \\( \\text{lcm}(1, 6) = 6 \\). Chi works every 7th school day, so her schedule is \\( \\text{lcm}(1, 7) = 7 \\).\n\nThe least common multiple of 3, 4, 6, and 7 is the smallest number that is a multiple of all four numbers. We calculate this as follows:\n\n1. First, we find the prime factorizations of each number:\n   - \\( 3 \\) is a prime number.\n   - \\( 4 = 2^2 \\)\n   - \\( 6 = 2 \\times 3 \\)\n   - \\( 7 \\) is a prime number.\n\n2. The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations:\n   - The highest power of 2 is \\( 2^2 \\).\n   - The highest power of 3 is \\( 3 \\).\n   - The highest power of 7 is \\( 7 \\).\n\n   Therefore, the LCM is:\n   \\[\n   2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 4 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 84\n   \\]\n\nSo, Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab \\(\\boxed{84}\\) school days from today.",
